  "result": "Perfect! All 139 tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support to the invoicing system.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** - Added new error code:\n   - `VOUCHER_EXISTS` - Invoice already has a voucher\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** - Added voucher functionality:\n   - `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })`:\n     - Validates invoice status is 'draft' (returns NOT_DRAFT otherwise)\n     - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID)\n     - Validates no voucher already exists (returns VOUCHER_EXISTS)\n     - Stores `{ code, amount }` on invoice.voucher\n     - Returns ok(newInvoice)\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals()` to:\n     - Include `voucher` field (0 if no voucher)\n     - Return `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher` (clamped at 0)\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js** - Added 8 comprehensive tests:\n   - Applying voucher to draft invoice\n   - Failing if invoice not draft\n   - Failing if voucher already exists\n   - Failing on invalid amounts (0, negative, decimal)\n   - Immutability verification\n   - invoiceTotals with voucher (deducted after VAT)\n   - invoiceTotals with voucher but no discount\n   - invoiceTotals returns zero voucher when none applied\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- Vouchers apply after VAT (subtotal - discount + vat - voucher)\n- One voucher per invoice maximum\n- Vouchers only apply to draft invoices (prevents modification after issuing)\n- Voucher amount is stored as-is without validation against total (caller responsible)\n- Total is clamped at 0 (vouchers can't create negative totals)",
